<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zviad Gamsakhurdia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a>–<a href="/years/1993">1993</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zviad Gamsakhurdia was a Georgian dissident writer and nationalist leader who became the first elected president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. His coalition won the Soviet Georgian elections of 1990, and Georgia declared independence on 9 April 1991, with him elected president the following month. His authoritarian rule provoked a civil war that ousted him in January 1992, and he died in 1993 after a failed attempt to return.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zviad-gamsakhurdia.jpg" alt="Zviad Gamsakhurdia" width="231" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George barateli by George Barateli in 1989 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zviad_Gamsakhurdia,_Tbilisi,_1988.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
